- public/models/manufacturing-core-full.glb and -lite.glb nodes: legacyshaft, approvedshaft, approvedhousing (or housing), legacyhousing (may appear: another producer is adding it; handle both names and absence gracefully but report which were used), legacybearing, legacyring, approvedbearing, approvedring. Metres; Blender export_yup: shaft-local (x, y, z) mm maps to glTF (x, z, -y) / 1000. Verify this mapping in a test from the GLB accessor bounds (approvedshaft spans glTF z from about -0.0715 to 0).

Requirements:
1. frame.ts: shaftLocalToStudy(out Matrix4) and helpers mapping shaft-local mm to study-root metres (the mapping above), plus the inverse; use them for camera, tools and progression setShaftTransform. The study root sits at a fixed world position/orientation (document the constant); never read hero.matrixWorld.
2. schedule.ts: pure, allocation-free sampleShaftSchedule(t, out) giving per-part opacity/visibility from shaftBeats: isolate 0-2 grooved blank (legacy shaft, all spaceDepth 0) fades in; shaping 2-15 shaper visible (fades in/out at the beat edges), legacy shaft progressing; materials 15-22.6 finished legacy shaft (depth 1) with warm stress from the script sampler; revised blank 22.6-25 axial wipe: a clipping plane perpendicular to the shaft axis sweeps along it, hiding the legacy shaft behind the wipe and revealing the approved shaft in its smooth-blank hobbing state (hobYc at infeed), same axis/datum, no overlapping translucent solids; hobbing 25-32 hob visible, approved shaft progressing, hob withdrawn by 32.0; runout hold 32-32.8 unobstructed, cool stress 32.8-35; supports 35-39 approved housing as a half-section (clipping plane through the axis, darker back-face material as the cap illusion), legacy bearing/ring shown as faint witnesses at the legacy pose, approved bearing and ring sliding as a rigid pair from the legacy pose to the approved pose (exactly +2.75 mm along the shaft axis, derived from the two exported node positions, asserting the delta in a test); finale 39-43 assembled study: approved shaft, bearing, ring, housing (section cap removed), plus planets and cages cloned per lifecycle-contract section 8 when ctx.rig provides the stage carriers (read src/scene/rig/nodeRoles.ts and TorqueWrenchHero.tsx around the planet rotation convention); they fade in and spin coherently with the shaft (planet multiplier convention from the rig). If the rig lacks carriers, keep the finale without them and report it in telemetry (finale.assembled false). Narrative alpha: fade out over 0-1.2 then 0 until Return (ownsNarrative true; returnBlend 0).
3. shaftRuntime.ts: createShaftRuntime(session, ctx) synchronous, returns runtime immediately with root and ready (fetch tier asset full or lite via ctx.tier, parse, stale checks, own resources). Instance-owned material clones (steel PBR, near-black studio), applyProgression on both shafts, stress overlay uniforms driven by the script sampler, tools from tools.ts placed each frame from the kinematics frame (cutter axis parallel to the shaft axis at centre distance SHAPER_CENTRE_DISTANCE_MM on azimuth MESH_AZ_RAD, axial position strokeCentreY, near edge at cutterRho, rotation cutterPhi; shaft rotation workPhi about its own axis; chip mesh from chip fields; hob axis perpendicular to the shaft tilted by the lead angle at hobToolA, axial hobYc, rotation hobPhi, shaft rotation hobWorkPhi; respect 'softened' by reducing repeated-feature contrast or fading the cutter teeth/gash detail). Camera: map ShaftCameraSample to world through the study frame into runtime.camera (valid true). Lighting: create the two lights inside the root (instance-owned), with the key following followWeight as the plan says. frame.discrete changes on beat changes only. RenderSample: near-black background, low env intensity, exposure per ring runtime conventions.
4. telemetry(out): write the shaft subtree from lifecycle-contract section 9 (teethFormed, teethPartial, cutter visible/stroke/infeed/rotation, hob visible/feed/rotation, card id/stamp from the script sampler, stress kind/mix, supports deltaYmm/witnesses/endpointHeld, finale assembled/shaftCount/racesFollow, narrative alpha) plus resources census; allocation-free (write into preallocated nested objects).
5. Tests (vitest, no WebGL): mapping matrix round trip and GLB bounds check (parse JSON chunk of the GLB file from disk); schedule purity/determinism under shuffled seeks and beat boundaries; part visibility rules above at dense times; tool placement math (cutter near edge distance to axis equals cutterRho within 1e-9 m; hob centre distance equals hobToolA); bearing/ring delta exactly 2.75 mm +-0.005 from exported node data; sample() allocation-free and pure (same digest after random seek order) using a runtime built against a stub ctx with the GLB parsed through a test helper if practical, otherwise test the pure sampling components and document what needs browser proof.

Verification: npx vitest run src/scene/inspection/shaft; npm run typecheck. Gate file: R1 frame mapping, R2 schedule and beats, R3 tools/progression wiring, R4 supports and finale, R5 telemetry, R6 purity/allocation, R7 tests/typecheck. Final message: changed paths, commands with results, what still needs browser proof, defects found in existing modules (file:line).
